# samples/04-BuiltInProcessors – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/04-BuiltInProcessors
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5104

### http-forward with a response template
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/42

### http-forward, relayed as it is (the fake CRM answers 404 above id 100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/101/raw

### The fake CRM itself – it wants the API key the forward endpoint adds
GET {{baseUrl}}/fake/crm/customers/42
X-Api-Key: fake-crm-key

### webhook: signed JSON payload, 202 once delivered
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ANV-1", "quantity": 2 }

### webhook to a flaky receiver: retried, "attempts": 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/flaky
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ROC-2" }

### What the receivers got
GET {{baseUrl}}/fake/webhooks

### response: a fixed body and a header
GET {{baseUrl}}/status

### response: request → 201 response
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "MAG-3", "quantity": 3 }

### response: text
GET {{baseUrl}}/motd?name=Ada

### sql-query: rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/products?minPrice=20

### sql-query: one row, or 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/products/MAG-3

### sql-query: a single value
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/stock-value

### Rejected on save: the host isn't allowed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "GET", "route": "/elsewhere", "processor": "http-forward", "processorConfig": { "url": "https://example.com/" } }

### Rejected on save: not a read-only statement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "GET", "route": "/wipe", "processor": "sql-query", "processorConfig": { "query": "DELETE FROM \"Products\"" } }
